3.1.evidence:
Second Part
P2TP2A
Article 32
(1) P2TP2A as referred to in Article 31 letter a, constitutes a service facility for the protection of women and children that is community-based which functions as an integrated service center in providing protection to women and children from violence.
(2) The membership composition of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) among others consists of:
a. elements of the Regional Government;
b. academics;
c. legal experts;
d. psychologists;
e. psychiatrists;
f. religious figures; and
g. community elements.
(3) The main duties of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) are: a. providing protection to women and children; and b. improving the quality of life of women and children.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment of P2TP2A shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

3.3.evidence:
Article 34
(1) The Village/Sub-District Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in Article 31 letter c, constitutes a functional work unit that organizes integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Village/Sub-District level.
(2) The Management of the Village/Sub-District Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. elements of Village/Sub-District apparatus;
b. elements of Village Non-Commissioned Officer Supervisor (Babinsa)/Sub-District;
c. elements of Community Non-Commissioned Officer Supervisor (Babinmas);
d. community leaders/religious leaders;
e. youth elements; and
f. elements of the Village/Sub-District PKK Mobilization Team
(3) The main duties of the Village/Sub-District Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of women and children protection;
b. receiving community complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Village/Sub-District area;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. socializing to the community about women and children protection; and
e. providing assistance for victims or referring to the Sub-District level women and children protection task force.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties and functions of the Village/Sub-District Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by the Decree of the Village Head/Sub-District Head.

